https://github.com/mlmed/torchxrayvision/blob/17726dd8f5e756eec3e5ae958281a289b05b1dae/torchxrayvision/utils.py
https://github.com/mlmed/torchxrayvision/blob/17726dd8f5e756eec3e5ae958281a289b05b1dae/torchxrayvision/datasets.py

Local changes and explicit research choices:

- Accept only verified, canonical single-frame stored pixels and a restricted
  CR/DX chest-input contract; load no upstream Python or dataset/download code.
- Normalize float32 samples with the unsigned BitsStored maximum (2^bits - 1),
  rather than each image's observed minimum/maximum. Resolve MONOCHROME1 once
  in stored space before normalization. Require identity modality rescale.
- Ignore DICOM VOI windows for this research input. The separate original-image
  viewer retains diagnostic-display window handling; its output is not model
  input. This choice does not establish equivalence to mixed training-dataset
  conversions, human presentation or population applicability.
- Preserve original padding along the background sampling path. Count padding
  separately in the source and crop; do not impute pixels or label it a lesion.
  Reject a crop with no varying valid samples.
- Use the author's integer-centered square crop and explicit CPU PyTorch
  224-by-224 bilinear interpolation with antialiasing and align_corners=False.
  Skip interpolation when already 224 square. Do not substitute the skimage
  resize path, rotate, flip or claim analysis of discarded source pixels.
- Permit only the declared 0.01 float32 interpolation-roundoff tolerance near
  the nominal normalized endpoints. Do not clip the resulting tensor; report
  its actual shape, range, source crop and valid/padding/discarded pixel counts.

This fixed profile is xrv_stored_range_v1. Numerical parity and synthetic smoke
checks provide engineering evidence only, not diagnostic accuracy, calibrated
disease probabilities, clinical validation or training-distribution equivalence.
